, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "New Interests and Aspirations", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Registering for the Course", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe  necessity, duty, advice, or strong dissaproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing Necessity in the Present and in the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modals <span class=\"italic\"> must </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have (got) to</span> to express necessity in the present and in the past. <br/> You use the negative forms of the modals <span class=\"italic\">need to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have to </span>to express absence of necessity in the present.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Must</span> refers to a necessary condition that comes from the subject and may be directed at the subject or the person the subject is talking to or about. It is used to express a strong necessity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: </br><ul><span class=\"italic\">First, you must present three pieces of ID.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have (got) to </span> refers to an obligation, which comes from someone / something other than the subject. This could be a rule or a regulation that the subject has no power to change. It expresses urgency and necessity, but to a lesser degree than<span class=\"italic\"> must </span> does.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: </br><ul><span class=\"italic\">If you want to pass this course, you have to keep on top of your assignments.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To express the absence of necessity, you use the <span class=\"strong\">negative form of have to</span>  (don't have to), not <span class=\"italic\"> mustn't</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">You don't have to select all your core subjects this semester.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can only express necessity in the past with the modal<span class=\"italic\"> have to</span>. <br/> Structure: <br/> <ul>subject + had to + infinitive", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/> <ul><span class=\"italic\">I had to drop out of one of my classes last semester.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can express the absence of necessity with the <span class=\"strong\">negative form of have to</span>  in the past. <br/> To do this, you use the structure: : <br/><ul> subject + didn't + have/need + infinitive.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:</br><ul><span class=\"italic\">Food and Beverage Management was an easy course. I didn't have to work too hard on that subject.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Absence of necessity can also be expressed by negative form of <span class=\"italic\">need</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "First you must present three pieces of ID and a document from your last school, as well as your student number.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do I have to have proof of address?", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I have selected the three core courses that I have to take.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I must inform you that, as of today, if you drop or withdraw from that course in particular ...", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Clarifying your opinion ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use linking expressions to express your position and to show how ideas are connected. You use linking expressions to clarify your opinion.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Discourse markers can show a <span class=\"strong\">connection </span>to what you want to say and what was said before. They can also show your position and opinion on a particular situation. <br/> Linking expressions are used to further explain and clarify your opinion or position on a subject. They follow a previous statement or sentence and build on that idea.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/> <ul><span class=\"italic\">By this I mean ... </span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"> I'm referring to ...</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">To be honest ...</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\">That is to say ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm referring to the transcript from your last school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "By that I mean that there are numerous reports, essays and seminars.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "To be honest I'm not sure if I should choose Food and Beverage Management because I took something similar at culinary school.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "transcript", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an \u200bexact written \u200bcopy of something, as in grades from University, college or high school", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You must present three pieces of ID and a transcript from your last school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about college and university.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "budgeting", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bprocess of \u200bcalculating how much \u200bmoney you must \u200bearn or \u200bsave during a particular \u200bperiod of \u200btime, and of \u200bplanning how you will \u200bspend it ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you take Food and Beverage you'll learn a lot about budgeting.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "proof of address", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an official paper that states your name and current address to prove where you live", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do I have to have proof of address?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to drop a course", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to officially say you will no longer be attending a class", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I must inform you that, as of today, if you drop that course in particular, you won't receive a refund.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "full course load", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the maximum number of courses you can take in a semester", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Many students have found it difficult to take a full course load when that course is part of it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "workload", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bamount of \u200bwork to be done, \u200bespecially by a \u200bparticular \u200bperson or \u200bmachine in a \u200bperiod of \u200btime", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Will you tell me which courses have the biggest work load?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "essay", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bshort \u200bpiece of writing on a \u200bparticular \u200bsubject, \u200bespecially one done by \u200bstudents as \u200bpart of the \u200bwork for a \u200bcourse ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That course has numerous reports, essays and seminars.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep on top of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to stay well-informed about the status of someone or something. ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to keep on top of your assignments and you must not get behind.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be all set", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be prepared, ready, or primed to begin or complete a task at hand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, you're all set!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to withdraw from a course", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to officially stop taking a course", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I must inform you that, as of today, if you withdraw from that course in particular, you won't receive a refund.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le04ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Select a course you would like to take abroad. Choose a country of your preference. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Surf  the Internet to find out what the registration process is and what the course requirements are. Write them down.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a presentation explaining the registration process and course requirements.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I read about education registration.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express what's necessary in registering for a school, college, etc.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the registration process and requirements for taking a course abroad.", "type": "text"}]}]}